# Styling: Angular Material + Tailwind

## Division of responsibility

- **Angular Material** — interactive, accessible UI primitives (buttons, form fields, dialogs, tables, navigation patterns). Follow current APIs and patterns from [Angular Material](https://material.angular.dev/).
- **Tailwind CSS** — layout, spacing, responsive behavior, and utility-level typography when it does not fight Material component internals. Use [Tailwind CSS documentation](https://tailwindcss.com/docs) as the source of truth for utilities and v4 usage.

## Global styles in this project

- **Material theming:** `src/material-theme.scss` — prefer Material 3 / theme tokens here instead of ad-hoc overrides scattered in components.
- **Tailwind entry:** `src/styles.css` — contains `@import 'tailwindcss';` and other global utilities.
- **Load order:** `angular.json` lists `material-theme.scss` **before** `styles.css`. Keep that order; put new global theme variables in the theme file and Tailwind-related globals in `styles.css` unless they are Material-specific.

## Conflict avoidance

- Avoid piling Tailwind classes onto Material components in ways that break their internal layout or focus rings.
- Do not rely on brittle `.mat-*` overrides; theme through `material-theme.scss` when possible.
- `::ng-deep` is a last resort — if used, add a short comment explaining why.

## Documentation and Browser MCP

When unsure about component APIs, theming, or Tailwind class behavior, **open the official docs with the Browser MCP** instead of guessing:

- [https://material.angular.dev/](https://material.angular.dev/)
- [https://tailwindcss.com/docs](https://tailwindcss.com/docs)

